         <div type="bio">
            <p>Scottish writer, theatre critic, and English translator of Henrik Ibsen’s plays. In 1900 upon the publication of eighteen-year-old Joyce’s review of Ibsen’s When We Dead Awaken in the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Fortnightly Review</name>, Archer corresponded with Joyce to convey Ibsen’s praise of and gratitude for the review. <hi rend="bold">Dirk Van Hulle</hi> and <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
